# Enterprise Three-Tier Hierarchical Network Design & Implementation

**Cisco Packet Tracer | Enterprise Networking | CCNA Practical Lab**

## Project Overview

This project focuses on the implementation of an enterprise-style three-tier hierarchical network architecture using Cisco Packet Tracer.

The network is structured around the Core, Distribution, and Access layers, connecting two separate office environments (Office A and Office B). The lab provides hands-on experience with enterprise networking concepts, network infrastructure design, redundancy, routing, network services, security, and wireless networking.

This project was completed as part of the **CCNA Mega Lab by Jeremy's IT Lab**.

## Network Architecture

The network follows a three-tier hierarchical architecture:

- **Core Layer:** Provides high-speed connectivity between network segments and acts as the central backbone.
- **Distribution Layer:** Handles inter-VLAN routing, redundancy, and policy-based network functions.
- **Access Layer:** Connects end devices and provides access to network resources.

The implementation includes two office environments connected through a centralized network infrastructure.

